    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="1029" n="935" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg935"/>

                <head>No. 567.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lewis to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 29, 1887</date>.
                        (Received April 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 88.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit inclosed an
                    official copy and translation thereof of the protocol of a treaty<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d567-f1"/> between Portugal and China. Whilst the former Government
                    has been in possession of Macoa for over three hundred years, there has never
                    been a treaty between the two countries.</p>
                <p>I am informed by Mr. Campbell, the agent for the Chinese Government, that the
                    treaty will be ratified in the course of the next three months.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. P. C. Lewis.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
